hadiths[473]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will certainly expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula, until I leave none but Muslims."""
"5027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will certainly drive some men away from my Basin, just as a stray camel is driven away from the herd."""
"5028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I certainly know people from my Ummah who will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds like the white mountains of Tihamah, and Allah Almighty will turn them into scattered dust. Listen! They will be your brothers and of your own kind; they will worship at night just as you do, but they will be people who, when alone with what Allah has made sacred, violate its sanctity."""
"5029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will meet Allah in a state in which I have not given anyone anything from anyone's wealth without his heartfelt consent. A sale is only by mutual consent."""
"5030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of His servant, when he turns to Him in repentance, than one of you who was on his mount in a desolate land and it escaped from him, carrying his food and drink. He despaired of it, then came to a tree and lay down in its shade, having despaired of his mount, when suddenly he saw it standing beside him. He took hold of its halter and then, out of the intensity of his joy, said: 'O Allah, You are my servant and I am Your Lord!' He made this mistake out of the intensity of his joy."""
"5031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of His servant than one of you who finds his camel that he had lost in a desolate land."""
"5032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of one of you than one of you is with his lost property when he finds it."""
"5033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of a servant than a man who stopped at a place where he faced the danger of death. With him was his mount carrying his food and drink. He laid down his head and fell asleep, and when he woke up his mount had gone. He kept searching for it until, when the heat and thirst became severe for him, he said: 'I will go back to the place where I was and sleep there until I die.' Then he raised his head, and there was his mount beside him, carrying his provisions, his food and his drink! So Allah Almighty is more pleased with the repentance of a believing servant than this man is with his mount and provisions."""
"5034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has far more power over you than you have over him."""
"5035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Treading on a live coal is dearer to me than treading on a grave."""
"5036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My sitting with a group of people who remember Allah Almighty from the Fajr prayer until the sun rises is dearer to me than freeing four slaves from the descendants of Isma'il; and my sitting with a group of people who remember Allah from the Asr prayer until the sun sets is dearer to me than freeing four slaves."""
"5037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My saying 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'wal-hamdu lillah' (and all praise is for Allah), 'wa la ilaha illallah' (and there is none worthy of worship except Allah) and 'wallahu akbar' (and Allah is the Greatest) is dearer to me than everything upon which the sun rises."""
"5038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Walking on a live coal or on a sword, or stitching my sandal to my foot, is dearer to me than walking on the grave of a Muslim; and it makes no difference to me whether I relieve myself in the middle of a grave or in the middle of the marketplace."""
"5039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A woman's praying in her room is better for her than praying in the courtyard; her praying in the courtyard is better than praying in the rest of the house; and her praying in the house is better than praying in the mosque."""
"5040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For one of you to take his rope, go to the mountain, gather firewood, sell it, eat from it and give charity is better for him than asking people."""
"5041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For one of you to take his rope, go to the mountain, bring a bundle of firewood on his back and sell it, whereby Allah Almighty preserves his dignity, is better for him than asking people, whether they give him or refuse him."""
"5042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For one of you to sit on a live coal until it burns through his clothes and reaches his skin is better for him than sitting on a grave."""
"5043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a man to commit adultery with ten women is a lesser sin than for him to commit adultery with the wife of his own neighbour; and for a man to steal from ten houses is easier (a lesser sin) than for him to steal from the house of his own neighbour."""
"5044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a man to step on a burning ember is better than for him to step on a grave."""
"5045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That an iron needle be driven into the head of one of you is better for him than that he should touch a woman who is not lawful for him."""
"5046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That one of you should go out early in the morning, carry firewood on his back, give charity from it and through it become free of need from people, is better for him than asking a man, whether he gives to him or refuses him. That is because the upper hand is better than the lower hand; and in spending, begin with those whom you support."""
"5047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For one of you to stand waiting for forty is better for him than to pass in front of a person who is praying."""
"5048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That the belly of one of you be filled with pus until it corrupts it is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."""
"5049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""That the belly of a man be filled with pus until it corrupts it is better for him than that it be filled with poetry."""
"5050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a man to give his land to his brother free of charge is better for him than to take a fixed rent for it."""
"5051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I know better than the Dajjal himself what the Dajjal will have with him: with the Dajjal there will be two flowing rivers; one of them will appear to the eye as white water, and the other will appear to the eye as blazing fire. So whoever of you encounters that, let him go to the river which appears to him as fire, then plunge into it, then lower his head and drink from it, for in reality it will be cold water. And indeed the Dajjal will be blotted out in the left eye (sightless), with a thick film over it. Between his eyes will be written 'Kafir' (disbeliever), which every believer will read, whether he knows how to read and write or not."""
"5052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I live until next year, I will certainly fast on the ninth (day)."""
"5053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I live, if Allah wills, I will certainly expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula."""
"5054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I live, if Allah wills, I will certainly forbid that anyone be named Rabah, Najih, Aflah or Yasar."""
"5055","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you are as you have said, then it is as though you are feeding them hot ashes, and as long as you remain in that state, there will remain with you a helper from Allah against them."""
"5056","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I will certainly forbid that anyone be named Nafi', Barakah or Yasar."""
"5057","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Here I am at Your service, O True God! Here I am at Your service."""
"5058","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Here I am at Your service, O Allah! Here I am at Your service. Indeed, the real good is the good of the Hereafter."""
"5059","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Here I am at Your service, O Allah! Here I am at Your service. Here I am at Your service; You have no partner. Here I am at Your service. Indeed, all praise, blessing and dominion belong to You alone; You have no partner."""
"5060","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The milk of a milch animal may be drawn in return for bearing its upkeep when it is held in pledge, and a riding animal may be ridden in return for bearing its upkeep when it is held in pledge; and the one who rides it and draws its milk is also responsible for its upkeep."""
"5061","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Learn your Hajj rites from me, for I do not know; perhaps I will not perform Hajj again after this Hajj of mine."""
"5062","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection every right will certainly be restored to its owner, to the extent that retribution will be taken for the hornless sheep from the horned sheep that butted it."""
"5063","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will certainly follow the ways of those who came before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, to the extent that if they had entered a lizard's hole, you too would enter it."" The Companions asked: ""Are the Jews and the Christians meant?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Who else then?"""
"5064","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the young unmarried girls, the women who keep in seclusion and the menstruating women certainly come out to the place of Eid prayer, and let them witness the good and the supplication of the Muslims; but the menstruating women should keep away from the place of prayer."""
"5065","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will certainly enter Paradise, except the one who refuses and runs away from Allah as a camel runs away."""
"5066","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Leave the prayer every month during the days of your menstruation, then perform ablution for every prayer, for this (blood) is merely the flow of a vein."""
"5067","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will certainly follow the ways of those who came before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, to the extent that if one of them entered a lizard's hole, you too would enter it, and if one of them had intercourse with his wife in the road, you too would do the same."""
"5068","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This Ummah will crowd around the Pond just as camels crowd that come to water on the fifth day."""
"5069","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group from my Ummah will certainly regard wine as lawful, calling it by another name."""
"5070","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You must certainly straighten your rows in your prayers, or else Allah will certainly put discord between your hearts."""
"5071","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of Muslims will certainly conquer the treasure of the family of Kisra (Chosroes) which is in the White Palace."""
"5072","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You must certainly straighten your rows, or else Allah will certainly put discord between your faces."""
"5073","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The earth will certainly be filled with injustice and oppression. Then, when it has been filled with injustice and oppression, Allah Almighty will send a man from my progeny whose name will be like my name and whose father's name will be like my father's name. He will fill the earth with justice and fairness just as it had been filled with injustice and oppression. Then the sky will not withhold any of its rain, nor will the earth withhold any of its produce. He will remain among you for seven or eight years, and if longer, then nine years."""
"5074","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The earth will certainly be filled with injustice and transgression; then a man from my Ahl al-Bayt (household) will certainly emerge, until he fills it with fairness and justice just as it had been filled with injustice and transgression."""
"5075","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The knots of Islam will certainly be undone one by one. Each time a knot is undone, people will cling firmly to the one that follows it. The first of them to be undone will be governance, and the last of them will be the prayer."""
"5076","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let her wait, in that month, for the number of nights and days that she used to menstruate before she was afflicted with this condition, and let her leave the prayer during that part of the month. Then, when that period has passed, let her take a ritual bath (ghusl), then bind a cloth, then pray."""
"5077","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The passing away of the world is a lighter matter in the sight of Allah than the killing of a Muslim man."""
"5078","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The passing away of the world is a lighter matter in the sight of Allah than the unjust killing of a believer."""
"5079","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not I who gave you mounts; rather, it is Allah who gave you mounts. And by Allah, if Allah wills, whenever I swear an oath and then see something else better than it, I do that which is better and make expiation for my oath."""
"5080","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I am not of the world, nor is the world of me. I and the Hour have been sent in such a way that we are racing to outstrip one another."""
"5081","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a thousand men."""
"5082","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a whole company."""
"5083","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps your lice have troubled you? Shave your head, and fast for three days and feed six poor people, or sacrifice a sheep."""
"5084","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps you are provided for because of him."""
"5085","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps you wish to return to Rifa'ah? No, that is not possible until you taste the sweetness of this other husband and he tastes your sweetness."""
"5086","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps you will encounter people who will offer the prayer outside its proper time. If you encounter them, then offer the prayer at its time, and then pray with them as well, and count it as a voluntary prayer."""
"5087","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps my intercession will benefit him on the Day of Resurrection, so that he is placed in a shallow part of the Fire that reaches his ankles, from which his brain will boil. (He said this about Abu Talib.)"""
"5088","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Perhaps, as long as these two branches do not dry out, the punishment will be lightened for the two of them."""
"5089","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who consumes usury (riba), the one who pays it, its witness and the one who writes it down."""
"5090","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who consumes usury (riba), the one who pays it, its two witnesses and the one who writes it down; they are all equal in this sin."""
"5091","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse wine, the one who drinks it, the one who serves it, the one who sells it, the one who buys it, the one who presses it, the one for whom it is pressed, the one who carries it, the one to whom it is carried, and the one who consumes its price."""
"5092","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the woman who, in grief for the deceased, scratches her face, tears open the neck of her garment and raises cries of woe and ruin."""
"5093","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who gives a bribe and the one who takes a bribe in judgement."""
"5094","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse usury (riba), the one who consumes it, the one who pays it, the one who writes it down and the one who witnesses it, while they know it; and may He also curse the woman who attaches hair extensions and the woman who has them attached, the woman who tattoos and the woman who has herself tattooed, and the woman who plucks eyebrows and the woman who has hers plucked."""
"5095","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the man who wears the clothing of women, and the woman who wears the clothing of men."""
"5096","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the woman among women who adopts the manner of men."""
"5097","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the thief: he steals an egg and his hand is cut off, and he steals a rope and his hand is cut off."""
"5098","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the scorpion; it spares neither the one who prays nor the one who does not. Kill it both outside the sanctuary (hill) and within the sanctuary (haram)."""
"5099","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the scorpion; it spares neither a prophet nor anyone else, but stings them."""
"5100","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the women who imitate men and the men who imitate women."""
"5101","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse both the one who performs halalah and the one for whom halalah is performed."""
"5102","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the male and female grave robber."""
"5103","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the men who adopt the manner of women and the women who adopt the manner of men."""
"5104","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the women who tattoo and those who have themselves tattooed, the women who pluck eyebrows and those who have theirs plucked, and the women who create gaps between their teeth for beauty, who alter the creation of Allah."""
"5105","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the woman who attaches hair extensions and the woman who has them attached, and the woman who tattoos and the woman who has herself tattooed."""
"5106","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."""
"5107","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the Jews. Allah forbade fat to them, so they sold it and consumed its price. And indeed, when Allah forbids a people to eat something, He also forbids its price to them."""
"5108","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the Jews and the Christians; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship."""
"5109","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the women who frequently visit graves."""
"5110","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who brands an animal on the face."""
"5111","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who reviles my Companions."""
"5112","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who curses his parents; may Allah Almighty curse the one who slaughters in the name of other than Allah; may Allah Almighty curse the one who gives refuge to an innovator; and may Allah Almighty curse the one who alters the boundary markers of the land."""
"5113","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May Allah Almighty curse the one who mutilates an animal."""
"5114","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May the curse of Allah be upon the one who gives a bribe and the one who takes a bribe."""
"5115","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A single going out in the path of Allah, in the morning or in the evening, is better than everything upon which the sun rises and sets; and a space in Paradise the length of a bow is better than everything upon which the sun rises and sets."""
"5116","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Going out in the path of Allah in the morning or the evening is better than the world and all that is in it; and a space in Paradise equal to the length of the bow of one of you, or the place of his whip, is better than the world and all that is in it. And if one of the women of the people of Paradise were to look down upon the earth, she would fill everything between the earth and the heavens with fragrance and would light it up; and even the veil on her head is better than the world and all that is in it."""
"5117","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It pleased me greatly that the time of the Muslims' prayer should be one, so much so that I resolved to send men into the houses to call people when the time of prayer came, and I even resolved to order men to stand on the fortresses and call the Muslims at the time of prayer."""
"5118","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has completed His argument against a servant whom He kept alive until he reached sixty or seventy years; indeed, Allah has completed the argument against him."""
"5119","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded so much to use the siwak that I began to fear for my teeth."""
"5120","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the whole world: from 'Indeed, We have granted you' up to 'great'."""
"5121","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Tonight a surah has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than everything upon which the sun rises: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory.'"""
"5122","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Musa has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud."""
"5123","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Abu Musa has been given some of the voices of the family of Dawud."""
"5124","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This man has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud."" (He meant Abu Musa.)"
"5125","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been harmed in the path of Allah as no one else has been harmed, and I have been made to fear in the path of Allah as no one else has been made to fear. Thirty days and nights passed over me when Bilal and I had nothing that a living creature could eat, except something that Bilal could hide under his armpit."""
"5126","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Jibril kept enjoining me about the neighbour so much that I thought he would make him an heir as well."""
"5127","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He has repented with such a repentance that, if all the people of Madinah were to repent likewise, it would be accepted from them."""
"5128","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This woman has repented with such a repentance that, if it were divided among seventy of the people of Madinah, it would suffice them all. And could there be a better repentance than that she gave up her life for the sake of Allah?"""
"5129","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have restricted something vast."""
"5130","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have restricted the vast mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah Almighty created one hundred mercies; of them He sent down one mercy by which the creatures, whether jinn, humans or animals, show compassion to one another, and with Him remain ninety-nine mercies. Do you say that he himself is more astray, or his camel?"""
"5131","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise was brought so near to me that, had I dared, I would have brought you some of its fruits; and the Fire was brought so near to me that I said: 'O Lord! Will I be among them too?' And I saw a woman being scratched by her cat. I asked: 'What is the matter with her?' It was said: 'She confined it until it died of hunger; she neither fed it nor let it go so that it could eat the creatures of the earth.'"""
"5132","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Just now, since I led you in prayer, I have seen Paradise and the Fire depicted before me in the qiblah side of this wall. I have never seen the like of this day in good and evil."""
"5133","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw the angels washing Hamzah."""
"5134","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw a man turning about at ease in Paradise on account of a tree that he had cut down from the middle of the road, which used to harm people."""
"5135","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I saw myself in the Hijr while Quraysh were asking me about my Night Journey. They asked me about things in Bayt al-Maqdis that I had not properly retained, and I was distressed as I had never been distressed before. Then Allah Almighty raised it up for me, and I began looking at it; whatever they asked me about, I informed them of it. And I saw myself among a group of the prophets: Musa was standing in prayer; he was a man with curly hair and of light build, as though he were one of the men of Shanu'ah. Isa bin Maryam was standing in prayer; the person who most resembled him was Urwah bin Mas'ud al-Thaqafi. Ibrahim was standing in prayer; the person who most resembled him was your companion, meaning myself. Then the time for prayer came and I led them in prayer. When I had finished the prayer, someone said: 'O Muhammad! This is Malik, the keeper of the Fire, so greet him with salam.' I turned towards him, and he greeted me with salam first."""
"5136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have asked me about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom Allah makes it easy: that you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the obligatory prayer, pay the obligatory zakah, fast in Ramadan and perform Hajj to the House. Shall I not tell you of the doors of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin just as water extinguishes fire, and so does a man's prayer in the middle of the night. Shall I not tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar and its peak? The head of the matter is Islam; whoever accepts Islam is safe. Its pillar is prayer, and its peak is jihad. Shall I not tell you of what holds all of that together? Restrain this"" - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed to his tongue. He said: ""O Prophet of Allah! Will we be taken to account for what we say?"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh! Does anything throw people into the Fire on their faces except the harvest of their tongues?"""
"5137","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Last night many women came to the household of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), each of them complaining of being beaten by her husband. By Allah! You will not find those men to be the best among you."""
"5138","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I recited this surah (Surah al-Rahman) to the jinn on the Night of the Jinn, and their response was better than yours. Whenever I reached the words of Allah, 'So which of the favours of your Lord will you both deny?', they would say: 'O our Lord! We deny none of Your favours; so to You belongs all praise.'"""
"5139","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After you, I said four phrases three times which, if they were weighed against all that you have said since this morning, would outweigh it: 'Subhan Allahi wa bihamdihi, 'adada khalqihi, wa rida nafsihi, wa zinata 'arshihi, wa midada kalimatihi' (Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him, as many times as the number of His creation, as much as pleases Him, as much as the weight of His Throne, and as much as the ink of His words)."""
"5140","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You have said a word which, if it were mixed with the water of the sea, would alter it."""
"5141","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have suffered much from your people, and the hardest of what I suffered from them was on the Day of Aqabah, when I presented myself to Ibn Abd Yalil bin Abd Kulal, and he did not respond to what I wanted. So I went away in a state of grief, and I did not come to myself until I had reached Qarn al-Tha'alib. I raised my head and saw a cloud shading me. I looked, and in it was Jibril. He called out to me and said: 'Allah Almighty has heard what your people said to you and how they answered you, and He has sent to you the Angel of the Mountains so that you may command him as you wish regarding them.' Then the Angel of the Mountains called out to me, greeted me with salam, and said: 'O Muhammad! It is just so; now command whatever you wish. If you wish, I will bring the two mountains together upon them.' I said: 'No, rather I hope that Allah Almighty will bring forth from their descendants people who will worship Allah alone and not associate anything with Him.'"""
"5142","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had resolved to order a man to lead the people in prayer, and then to set fire to the houses of those men who stay away from the Friday prayer."""
"5143","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had resolved to send for Abu Bakr and make a covenant (of succession) concerning him, so that no one would say anything or any wisher wish for anything. Then I said: Allah refuses it, and the believers will not accept it."""
"5144","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had resolved to curse him with a curse that would enter his grave with him. How can he make him an heir when that is not lawful for him? How can he use him as a servant when that is not lawful for him?!"""
"5145","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had resolved to forbid ghilah, until I remembered that the Romans and the Persians do that, and it does not harm their children."""
"5146","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I had resolved not to accept a gift from anyone except a man of Quraysh, an Ansari, a man of Thaqif or a man of Daws."""
"5147","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The heart of the son of Adam turns over more rapidly than a cooking pot that is boiling vigorously."""
"5148","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying to say 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah)."""
"5149","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying to say 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah), for the soul of the believer departs easily, like sweat, while the soul of the disbeliever departs from the side of his jaw, just as the soul of a donkey departs."""
"5150","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Prompt your dying to say 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah), for whoever's last words at the time of death are 'La ilaha illallah' will certainly enter Paradise one day or another, whatever may have befallen him before that."""
"5151","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a man to stand in the ranks in the path of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, for one hour is better than sixty years of worship."""
"5152","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Night Journey (Mi'raj), I met Ibrahim, and he said: 'O Muhammad, convey my greetings of peace to your Ummah, and tell them that Paradise has pure soil and sweet water, that it consists of level plains, and that its plants are 'Subhan Allah' (Glory be to Allah), 'Wal-hamdu lillah' (and praise be to Allah), 'Wa la ilaha illallah' (and there is no true god except Allah) and 'Wallahu akbar' (and Allah is the Greatest).'"""
"5153","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A portion of Paradise the size of the space taken by the whip of one of you is better than everything between the heavens and the earth."""
"5154","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In return for it you will have seven hundred she-camels with nose-reins in Paradise."""
"5155","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In return for it you will have, on the Day of Resurrection, seven hundred she-camels, all of them with nose-reins."""
"5156","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is a reward for you in (helping) every thirsty living creature that has a moist liver."""
"5157","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Yazid, you have what you intended; and O Ma'n, you have what you took."""
"5158","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For you, the people of the ship, there are two emigrations (hijrahs)."""
"5159","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For you is every bone over which the name of Allah has been mentioned; it will come into your hands as full of meat as it can be, and every piece of dung is fodder for your animals. So do not clean yourselves after relieving yourselves (istinja) with these two, for they are the food of your brothers."""
"5160","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""But for you the best and most beautiful jihad is an accepted Hajj (Hajj mabrur)."""
"5161","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every son of Adam has had his share of zina written for him. The zina of the eye is looking, the zina of the tongue is speaking, the two ears commit zina and their zina is listening, the two hands commit zina and their zina is grasping, the two feet commit zina and their zina is walking, and the mouth commits zina and its zina is kissing."""
"5162","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every Ummah has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of my Ummah is Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah."""
"5163","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every Ummah has its Magians (deniers of predestination), and the Magians of my Ummah are those who say there is no predestination (qadar). If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."""
"5164","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every disease there is a remedy, so when the right remedy for the disease is found, recovery comes by the permission of Allah Almighty."""
"5165","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every surah has its share of bowing (ruku') and prostration (sujud)."""
"5166","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every mistake (sahw) there are two prostrations after giving the salam."""
"5167","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every betrayer, a banner will be set up behind him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5168","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every betrayer there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection by which he will be recognised."""
"5169","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every betrayer a banner will be set up in proportion to his betrayal."""
"5170","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For every betrayer, a banner will be raised on the Day of Resurrection in proportion to his betrayal. Listen! There is no betrayer greater in betrayal than a ruler over the common people."""
"5171","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every generation has some who excel and lead the way."""
"5172","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In every generation of my Ummah there are some who excel and lead the way."""
"5173","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a legacy and an estate that he leaves behind, and my legacy and my estate are the Ansar, so look after them for my sake."""
"5174","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet had a supplication which he made for his Ummah and it was answered for him, and I wish, if Allah wills (in sha' Allah), to save my supplication as intercession for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5175","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication which he made for his Ummah, and I have kept my supplication hidden away as intercession for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5176","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication that is answered, and every prophet hastened to make his supplication, but I have kept my supplication hidden away as intercession for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection. So it will reach, if Allah wills (in sha' Allah), every person of my Ummah who dies without associating anything with Allah."""
"5177","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has a supplication which he makes, and I wish to keep my supplication hidden away as intercession for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5178","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every prophet has an answered supplication which he makes, and it is answered for him and granted to him, and I have kept my supplication hidden away as intercession for my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5179","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets a sixth, and whatever remains goes to the sister."""
"5180","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a virgin (bride) there are seven days, and for a previously married woman there are three days."""
"5181","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is a door of repentance in the direction of the west, the width of which is a journey of seventy years. It will remain open like this until one of the signs of your Lord comes, namely the rising of the sun from the west."""
"5182","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The martyr has seven qualities with Allah: he is forgiven with the very first drop of his blood; he is shown his place in Paradise; he is clothed in the garment of faith; he is married to seventy-two wives from among the Hur al-Ayn (wide-eyed maidens of Paradise); he is protected from the punishment of the grave; he is kept safe from the Greatest Terror; a crown of dignity is placed on his head, a single ruby of which is better than the world and everything in it; and he is granted intercession for seventy people of his household."""
"5183","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fasting person has two joys: one joy when he breaks his fast, and another joy when he meets his Lord."""
"5184","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For those who fast there is a gate in Paradise called 'al-Rayyan'. No one other than them will enter through it. When the last of them has entered, it will be closed. Whoever enters through it will drink, and whoever drinks will never feel thirst again."""
"5185","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the righteous slave there is a double reward."""
"5186","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who goes out to fight has his reward, and the one who equips and sends him has his own reward as well as the reward of the one who fights."""
"5187","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who suffers seasickness at sea has the reward of one martyr, and the one who drowns has the reward of two martyrs."""
"5188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer has six rights over the believer: to visit him when he is ill, to attend his funeral when he dies, to accept his invitation when he invites him, to greet him with salam when he meets him, to say 'Yarhamuk Allah' (May Allah have mercy on you) when he sneezes, and to be sincere towards him both in his absence and in his presence."""
"5189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For wiping over leather socks (khuffs), the traveller has three days and their nights, and the resident has one day and one night."""
"5190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Muslim has four rights over the Muslim: to say 'Yarhamuk Allah' (May Allah have mercy on you) when he sneezes, to accept his invitation when he invites him, to attend his funeral when he dies, and to visit him when he is ill."""
"5191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is the right of the slave to be given food and clothing in a fitting manner, and not to be burdened with any work except what he can bear."""
"5192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is the right of the slave to be given food and clothing, and not to be burdened with any work except what he can bear. If you give them heavy work, then help them, and do not torment the servants of Allah, who are a creation just like you."""
"5193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the Muhajirun, staying in Makkah for three days after returning from Hajj is permissible."""
"5194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I did not forbid weeping; rather, I forbade two foolish and sinful sounds: a sound at a time of joy and play, to the tune of Satan's flute, and a sound at a time of calamity, in the form of scratching faces, tearing garments and the shrieking of Satan. As for tears flowing from the eyes, that is mercy."""
"5195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Jews do not envy us for anything as much as they envy us for the greeting of salam and for saying Amin."""
"5196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The spoils of war were not made lawful for anyone among the black-headed ones before you; they would be gathered, and fire would descend from the sky and consume them."""
"5197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty did not send any prophet except in the language of his people."""
"5198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing remains of prophethood except the things that bring glad tidings, that is, righteous dreams."""
"5199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None spoke in the cradle except three: Isa (peace be upon him). And among the Children of Israel there was a man called Jurayj. He was praying when his mother came and called him. He thought: 'Shall I answer her or continue praying?' So his mother said: 'O Allah, do not let him die until You show him the faces of prostitutes.' Jurayj was in a hermitage, and a woman tried to tempt him and spoke to him, but he refused. So she went to a shepherd and gave herself to him, and she gave birth to a boy and said: 'This is Jurayj's child.' The people came to him, broke down his hermitage, brought him down and reviled him. He performed ablution and prayed, then came to the child and asked: 'O boy, who is your father?' He said: 'The shepherd.' The people said: 'We will build your hermitage of gold.' He said: 'No, build it only of clay.' And a woman of the Children of Israel was nursing her son when a distinguished rider passed by her, and she said: 'O Allah, make my son like him.' The child left the breast, turned towards the rider and said: 'O Allah, do not make me like him.' Then he went back to nursing. Then a slave woman passed by, and the mother said: 'O Allah, do not make my son like her.' The child left the breast and said: 'O Allah, make me like her.' The mother asked: 'Why is that?' The child said: 'That rider was one of the tyrants, and as for this slave woman, people say she stole and committed adultery, yet she did none of that.'"""
"5200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing has been seen like marriage for those who love one another."""
"5201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No prophet was buried anywhere other than the place where he died."""
"5202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibrahim (peace be upon him) told only three lies, two of them for the sake of Allah: his saying, 'I am sick,' and his saying, 'Rather, this biggest of them did it.' And one day Ibrahim and Sarah were travelling when they came upon one of the tyrants, and he was told: 'Here is a man who has with him a most beautiful woman.' He sent for Ibrahim and asked him about her, saying: 'Who is this?' He said: 'She is my sister.' Then Ibrahim came to Sarah and said: 'O Sarah, there is no believer on the face of the earth besides me and you, and this man asked me about you and I told him that you are my sister, so do not contradict me.' Then he sent for Sarah, and when she went in to him, he began to reach out his hand towards her, and he was seized. He said: 'Pray to Allah for me and I will not harm you.' Sarah prayed to Allah and he was released. Then he reached out his hand towards her a second time and was seized as before or even more severely. He said: 'Pray to Allah for me and I will not harm you.' Sarah prayed and he was released. Then he called one of his gatekeepers and said: 'You have not brought me a human being; you have brought me a devil!' Then he gave her Hajar to serve her. Sarah came to Ibrahim while he was standing in prayer, and he asked with a gesture of his hand: 'What happened?' Sarah said: 'Allah has turned the scheme of the wicked man back upon his own throat, and has given me Hajar to serve me.'"""
"5203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who conveys good words between two people in order to reconcile them is not counted a liar."""
"5204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No people withhold the zakah of their wealth except that they are deprived of rain from the sky, and were it not for the animals, they would not be given rain at all."""
"5205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When your brothers were martyred on the day of Uhud, Allah Almighty placed their souls in the bellies of green birds. They go to the rivers of Paradise, eat of its fruits, and settle in lamps of gold hanging in the shade of the Throne. When they found how excellent their food, their drink and their place of rest were, they said: 'If only someone would convey to our brothers on our behalf that we are alive in Paradise and are being given provision, so that they do not lose interest in jihad and do not hold back at the time of battle.' Allah Almighty said: 'I Myself will convey it to them on your behalf.'"""
"5206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty drowned Pharaoh, he said: 'I believe that there is no god except the One in whom the Children of Israel believe.' Jibril said: 'O Muhammad, if only you had seen me as I took mud from the sea and stuffed it into his mouth, fearing that mercy might reach him.'"""
"5207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Adam (peace be upon him) died, the angels washed him with water an odd number of times and dug a niche grave (lahd) for him, and they said: 'This is the practice of Adam (peace be upon him), which will remain among his descendants.'"""
"5208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty created Adam, He passed His hand over his back, and every soul He was to create until the Day of Resurrection fell from his back. Then He placed a gleam of light between the eyes of every human being among them, then presented them to Adam. Adam asked: 'O Lord, who are these?' He said: 'These are your descendants.' Adam saw a man among them, the light between whose eyes pleased him greatly, and he asked: 'O Lord, who is this?' He said: 'A man from your descendants, from the last of the nations, who will be called Dawud.' Adam asked: 'O Lord, how long is his life?' He said: 'Sixty years.' Adam said: 'Then add forty years to it from my life.' He said: 'Then this decision will be written and sealed, and it will not be changed.' When Adam's appointed life came to an end, the Angel of Death came. Adam said: 'Do forty years of my life not remain?' The angel said: 'Did you not give them to your son Dawud?' Adam denied it, and so his descendants learned to deny; Adam forgot, and so his descendants became forgetful; and Adam erred, and so his descendants began to err."""
"5209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty created Adam and breathed the soul into him, he sneezed and said: 'Al-hamdu lillah' (All praise is for Allah), and so he praised Allah by His permission. His Lord said to him: 'Yarhamuka Allah ya Adam' (O Adam, may Allah have mercy on you)! Go to those angels sitting in a gathering and say: 'As-salamu alaykum' (Peace be upon you).' They said: 'Wa alayka as-salamu wa rahmatullah' (And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah). Then Adam returned to his Lord, and Allah said: 'This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants among themselves.' Then Allah Almighty, while both His hands were closed, said to Adam: 'Choose whichever you wish.' Adam said: 'I choose the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are blessed and right.' Then Allah opened it, and in it were Adam and his descendants. Adam asked: 'O Lord, who are these?' He said: 'These are your descendants.' The life span of every human being was written between his eyes, and among them was a man who was among the most radiant of them. Adam asked: 'O Lord, who is this?' He said: 'This is your son Dawud, and I have written for him a life of forty years.' Adam said: 'O Lord, increase his life.' He said: 'That is what has been written for him.' Adam said: 'O Lord, then I have given him sixty years of my life.' He said: 'It is up to you.' Then Adam was made to dwell in Paradise for as long as Allah willed, then he was sent down from it. Adam used to keep count of his own life. Then the Angel of Death came to him, and Adam said to him: 'You have come early; a thousand years were written for me.' The angel said: 'Yes, but you gave sixty years to your son Dawud.' Adam denied it, and so his descendants learned to deny; he forgot, and so his descendants became forgetful. From that day, writing and witnesses were commanded."""
"5210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty created Paradise, He said to Jibril: 'Go and look at it.' He went and looked at it, then came and said: 'O Lord, by Your might, whoever hears of it will surely wish to enter it.' Then Allah surrounded it with hardships, then said: 'O Jibril, go and look at it now.' He went, looked at it, then came and said: 'O Lord, by Your might, I now fear that no one will be able to enter it.' Then, when Allah Almighty created Hell, He said: 'O Jibril, go and look at it.' He went, looked at it, then came and said: 'By Your might, whoever hears of it will not wish to enter it.' Then Allah surrounded it with desires, then said: 'O Jibril, go and look at it now.' He went, looked at it, then said: 'O Lord, by Your might, I now fear that no one will escape it and that all will enter it.'"""
"5211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty gave Adam his form in Paradise, He left him for as long as Allah willed. Iblis began to circle around him, looking at him, and when he saw that he was hollow inside, he knew that this was a creation that would not be able to control itself."""
"5212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When I was taken up on the Mi'raj, I saw Idris (peace be upon him) in the fourth heaven."""
"5213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, took me up on the Mi'raj, I passed by people who had nails of copper with which they were scratching their faces and chests. I asked: 'O Jibril, who are these?' He said: 'These are the people who eat the flesh of others and attack their honour.'"""
"5214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty created the creation, He wrote in His Book, which is with Him above the Throne: 'Indeed, My mercy prevails over My wrath.'"""
"5215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When I was taken on the night journey to Bayt al-Maqdis and Quraysh disbelieved me, I stood in the Hatim, and Allah Almighty displayed Bayt al-Maqdis before me, so I began telling them about its features while I was looking at it."""
"5216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the soul was breathed into Adam, it ran through his body and flew until it reached his head. He sneezed and said: 'Al-hamdu lillahi rabbil-alamin' (All praise is for Allah, the Lord of all the worlds). Allah Almighty said: 'Yarhamuka Allah' (May Allah have mercy on you)."""
"5217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will not recite anything, in the sight of Allah, greater than 'Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.'"""
"5218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""As long as the disbelievers are fought, emigration (hijrah) will never come to an end."""
"5219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will keep on asking: 'This is Allah, the Creator of everything; then who created Allah?'"""
"5220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This religion will always remain established, with a group of Muslims fighting for its sake, until the Hour is established."""
"5221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will never combine two swords upon this Ummah: a sword from within it and a sword from its enemy."""
"5222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one's deeds will admit him into Paradise, not even me, unless Allah covers me with the grace of His mercy. So keep to the right path and stay close to it. And let none of you wish for death: if he is a doer of good, perhaps his good will increase, and if he is a wrongdoer, perhaps he will repent and seek Allah's pleasure."""
"5223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man who took part in Badr and al-Hudaybiyah will never enter Hell."""
"5224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty will not leave this Ummah unable to attain His promise, even for half a day."""
"5225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A people who entrust their affairs to a woman will never prosper."""
"5226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who practises soothsaying, or seeks his fortune by divining arrows, or turns back from a journey out of an evil omen, will not enter the high ranks."""
"5227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one who took part in Badr or the Pledge of Ridwan will enter Hell."""
"5228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one who prays before the rising of the sun and before its setting will enter Hell."""
"5229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""None of you will be saved by his deeds, not even me, unless Allah covers me with His mercy. But keep to the right path and stay close to it, and set out in the morning, in the evening and in part of the night; and moderation, moderation, and you will reach your goal."""
"5230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No servant will come on the Day of Resurrection saying 'La ilaha illallah' (There is no true god except Allah), seeking by it the Face of Allah, except that Allah will make Hell forbidden for him."""
"5231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will not be destroyed until they have left themselves without excuse."""
"5232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The banner of the one who betrays a covenant will be set up behind him on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If ten men of the Jews had believed in me, all the Jews would have believed in me."""
"5234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you had taken its skin, water and acacia leaves would have purified it."""
"5235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you were to commit so many sins that your sins reached the sky, and then you repented, Allah would surely accept your repentance."""
"5236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even if the morning had grown later than it has, I would still have prayed these two rak'ahs and performed them well and beautifully."" (The two sunnah rak'ahs of Fajr were meant.)"
"5237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had you given it to your maternal relatives, it would have been greater for your reward."""
"5238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If anyone could escape the squeezing of the grave, this child would surely have escaped it."""
"5239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband."""
"5240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the son of Adam were to flee from his provision as he flees from death, his provision would overtake him just as death overtakes him."""
"5241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If, when one of you intends to go to his wife, he says: 'Bismillah, Allahumma jannibna ash-shaytan wa jannib ash-shaytan ma razaqtana' (In the name of Allah. O Allah, keep Satan away from us and keep Satan away from what You grant us), then if a child is decreed for them from that union, Satan will never harm it."""
"5242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If, when one of you stops at a place, he says: 'A'udhu bi kalimatillahi at-tammati min sharri ma khalaq' (I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created), nothing will harm him in that place until he departs from it."""
"5243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the servants did not sin, Allah Almighty would create a creation that would sin, then seek forgiveness, and then He would forgive them; and He is the Most Forgiving, the Most Merciful."""
"5244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Allah were to punish the inhabitants of His heavens and the inhabitants of His earth, He could punish them and He would not be unjust to them; and if He were to have mercy on them, His mercy would be far better for them than their deeds. And if you were to spend gold equal to (the mountain of) Uhud in the way of Allah, Allah would not accept it from you until you believe in divine decree (qadr) and know that whatever has befallen you was never going to miss you, and whatever has missed you was never going to befall you. And if you were to die upon anything other than this belief, you would enter the Fire."""
"5245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the fluid from which a child is created were poured out onto a rock, Allah Almighty would bring forth a child even from it; and Allah Almighty will certainly create any soul that He is to create."""
"5246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a man looks into your home without permission and you throw a pebble at him and put out his eye, there is no sin upon you."""
"5247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth all took part together in (shedding) the blood of a believer, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, would throw them face down into Hell."""
"5248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a stone the size of seven pregnant she-camels were dropped from the edge of Hell, it would keep falling into it for seventy years and would not reach its bottom."""
"5249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a man were to be dragged on his face from the day he was born until the day he dies in old age, for the pleasure of Allah, he would still regard it as insignificant on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a single drop of Zaqqum were dripped into this world, it would ruin the livelihoods of the people of the world; so what then of the one whose very food it is?"""
"5251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If even as much as a fingernail could carry of what is in Paradise were to appear, everything between the edges of the heavens and the earth would be adorned by it. And if a man from the people of Paradise were to look out and his bracelets appeared, they would eclipse the light of the sun just as the sun eclipses the light of the stars."""
"5252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If, when you leave my company, you remained in the same state that you are in here, the angels would shake hands with you in the streets of Madinah."""
"5253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you remained at all times in the same state that you are in when you are with me, the angels would shake hands with you with their palms and would visit you in your homes. And if you did not sin, Allah would bring a people who would sin so that He might forgive them."""
"5254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you were to rely upon Allah Almighty as He truly deserves to be relied upon, He would provide for you just as He provides for the birds: they go out in the morning with empty stomachs and return in the evening with full bellies."""
"5255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had I known beforehand what I have come to know afterwards, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal with me and I would have made it an Umrah. So whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him leave the state of ihram and make it an Umrah."""
"5256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had I known beforehand what I came to know afterwards, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal with me; and were it not that I have the sacrificial animal with me, I would have left the state of ihram."""
"5257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were given a sheep's trotter as a gift, I would accept it; and if I were invited to (a meal of) it, I would accept."""
"5258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If only we had left this door for the women."""
"5259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If a woman knew the right of her husband, she would not sit while his morning or evening meal is present until he has finished it."""
"5260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew the extent of Allah's mercy, you would rely upon it alone."""
"5261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what has been stored up for you, you would not grieve over what has been withheld from you."""
"5262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little, and you would go out into the roads crying out to Allah Almighty."""
"5263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."""
"5264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what (virtue) there is in the first row, there would be no way (to settle it) except by drawing lots."""
"5265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what (reward) there is for you with Allah, you would love for your poverty and need to increase even more."""
"5266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the Qur'an were gathered in a piece of leather, Allah Almighty would not burn it with the Fire."""
"5267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If only you would go out to our camels and drink of their milk and their urine."""
"5268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were invited to (a meal of) a sheep's foreleg or trotter, I would accept; and if I were given a foreleg or a trotter as a gift, I would accept it."""
"5269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If he had come near me, the angels would have snatched him away limb by limb. (This referred to Abu Jahl.)"""
"5270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If only you had seen me as I was listening to your recitation last night, (you would have known that) you have been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud (i.e. a voice like theirs)."""
"5271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to stone anyone without evidence, I would have stoned this woman."""
"5272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had Ibrahim lived, he would have been a truthful one (siddiq) and a prophet."""
"5273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had I known that you were looking, I would have poked this pin into your eye. Seeking permission has been prescribed only for the sake of (guarding) the sight."""
"5274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you were forgiven for the (wrongs) you do to animals, a great deal would be forgiven you."""
"5275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If it had been decreed, it would have happened."""
"5276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had you said 'Bismillah' (In the name of Allah), the angels would have lifted you up while the people watched you, until they took you into the expanse of the sky."""
"5277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had I said 'Yes', it would have become obligatory; and had it become obligatory, you would not have been able to carry it out; and had you not been able to carry it out, you would have been punished."""
"5278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had you said this word when you were in control of your own affair, you would have attained complete success."""
"5279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Usamah were a girl, I would have clothed him and adorned him (with jewellery) until I had him sought after in marriage."""
"5280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even if faith were at the Pleiades (star cluster), some men from Persia would surely attain it."""
"5281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If faith were at the Pleiades, a man from the sons of Persia would go there until he attained it."""
"5282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the Qur'an were (kept) in a piece of leather, the Fire would not consume it."""
"5283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If al-Mut'im bin Adi were alive and then spoke to me on behalf of these foul ones (i.e. the captives of Badr), I would have released them for his sake."""
"5284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If there were to be a prophet after me, it would have been Umar bin al-Khattab."""
"5285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If this (breastfeeding during pregnancy) were harmful, it would certainly have harmed Persia and Rome."""
"5286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If anything could outstrip divine decree, the evil eye would outstrip it."""
"5287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If anything could outstrip divine decree, the evil eye would outstrip it. And when you are asked to wash (for someone afflicted by it), then wash."""
"5288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would desire a second one along with it; and if he had two valleys, he would desire a third along with them. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."""
"5289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the son of Adam had a valley of date palms, he would wish for another like it, then wish for another like it, until he wishes for many valleys. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust."""
"5290","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I had gold equal to (the mountain of) Uhud, it would please me that three days should not pass over it while any of it remained with me, except something I set aside for paying off a debt."""
"5291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had he been a Muslim, and you freed a slave on his behalf, or gave charity on his behalf, or performed Hajj on his behalf, that would have reached him."""
"5292","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If this world were worth even the wing of a mosquito to Allah, He would not give a disbeliever even a single sip of water from it."""
"5293","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If one surah (alone) were to suffice, this surah would have sufficed people."""
"5294","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband."""
"5295","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to command anyone to prostrate to other than Allah, I would have commanded the woman to prostrate to her husband. By the One in whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad! A woman does not fulfil the right of her Lord until she fulfils the entire right of her husband, so much so that if he asks her for herself while she is on a camel's saddle, she should not refuse him."""
"5296","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to take anyone from the people of the earth as a close friend, I would have taken Ibn Abi Quhafah as a close friend; but your companion is the Khalil (intimate friend) of Allah."""
"5297","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to take anyone from my Ummah as a close friend besides my Lord, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend; but he is my brother and my companion."""
"5298","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If I were to take anyone as a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend; but he is my brother and my companion, and Allah has taken your companion as His Khalil."""
"5299","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Even if you were scooping from (the valley of) Buthan, you would not have given any more."""
"5300","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had I not embraced it, it would have kept weeping until the Day of Resurrection."""
"5301","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you did not commit sins, Allah Almighty would bring a people who would commit sins so that He might forgive them."""
"5302","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had you not measured it, you would have kept eating from it and it would have lasted for you."""
"5303","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you did not commit sins, I would fear for you something greater than that: vanity, vanity (self-admiration)."""
"5304","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If only one day of this world remained, Allah would lengthen that day until He sends in it a man from my household whose name matches my name and whose father's name matches my father's name. He will fill the earth with equity and justice just as it had been filled with oppression and tyranny."""
"5305","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If only one day of time remained, Allah would send a man from my household who will fill it with justice just as it had been filled with oppression."""
"5306","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If anyone could escape the squeeze of the grave, Sa'd bin Mu'adh would have escaped it. He was squeezed once, then it was relieved from him."""
"5307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If anyone could escape the squeeze of the grave, this child would have escaped it."""
"5308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If Musa were to descend and you followed him and abandoned me, you would go astray. I am your share among the prophets, and you are my share among the nations."""
"5309","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid that it is from the charity (sadaqah), I would have eaten it."""
"5310","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man from the Ansar. And if the people were to go through a valley or a mountain pass, I would go through the valley of the Ansar and their mountain pass."""
"5311","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not for the Hijrah, I would have been a man from the Ansar. And if the people were to go through a valley or a mountain pass, I would be with the Ansar."""
"5312","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to the believers, I would have commanded them to delay the Isha prayer and to use the miswak at every prayer."""
"5313","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have commanded them to delay the Isha prayer until a third of the night or half of it."""
"5314","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have commanded them to pray it (i.e. the Isha prayer) like this, at midnight."""
"5315","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the miswak at every prayer."""
"5316","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the miswak at every prayer, and I would have delayed the Isha prayer until a third of the night."""
"5317","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have commanded them to use the miswak with every ablution."""
"5318","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have commanded them to perform ablution for every prayer and to use the miswak with every ablution."""
"5319","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid of causing hardship to my Ummah, I would have made the miswak obligatory upon them along with ablution, and I would have delayed the Isha prayer until midnight."""
"5320","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that envoys are not killed, I would have struck off both your necks."""
"5321","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that dogs are a nation (a community among the creatures), I would have commanded that they be killed. So kill every jet-black one among them. And there is no household that keeps a dog except that a qirat is deducted from their deeds every day, except a hunting dog, a farm dog, or a dog that guards sheep."""
"5322","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that dogs are a nation, I would have commanded that all of them be killed. So kill the jet-black one among them."""
"5323","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that the people have only recently come out of disbelief, and that I do not have the funds that would suffice for its construction, I would have included five cubits of the Hatim in it, and I would have made for it a door through which people enter and a door through which they exit."""
"5324","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were I not afraid that Safiyyah would feel (pain) in her heart, I would have left him (Hamzah) as he is, until the beasts and birds ate him and he would be raised from their bellies."""
"5325","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that you would stop burying one another, I would have supplicated to Allah to let you hear the punishment of the grave."""
"5326","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that your people have only recently come out of Jahiliyyah (the pre-Islamic ignorance), I would have demolished the Ka'bah and made two doors for it."""
"5327","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that your people have only recently come out of Jahiliyyah, I would have spent the treasure of the Ka'bah in the path of Allah, made its door level with the ground, and included (a part) of the Hatim in it."""
"5328","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were you not an envoy, I would have struck off your neck."""
"5329","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you did not commit sins, Allah would create a creation who would commit sins so that He might forgive them."""
"5330","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not for the Children of Israel, food would not spoil and meat would not rot; and were it not for Hawwa (Eve), no woman would betray her husband."""
"5331","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not that your people have only recently come out of disbelief, I would have demolished the House and rebuilt it on the foundations of Ibrahim, and I would have made a door for it at the back as well, for when Quraysh built the House, they cut it short."""
"5332","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the sickness of the sick, I would have delayed the Isha prayer."""
"5333","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had this not (already) been decreed in the Book of Allah, the matter between me and her would have been different."""
"5334","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Had the Black Stone not been touched by the impurities of Jahiliyyah, any sick person who touched it would have been cured; and there is nothing on earth from Paradise other than it."""
"5335","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If people were given (their claims) on the basis of their claims alone, some people would claim the blood and wealth of others; but the oath is upon the one against whom the claim is made."""
"5336","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the one who drinks while standing knew what is in his stomach, he would make himself vomit."""
"5337","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the one who passes in front of a person praying knew what (sin) is upon him, standing for forty would be better for him than passing in front of him."""
"5338","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the believer knew the punishment that is with Allah, no one would hope for Paradise; and if the disbeliever knew the mercy that is with Allah, no one would despair of Paradise."""
"5339","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If people knew what (reward) there is in the call to prayer (adhan) and the first row, and then found no way but to draw lots for it, they would draw lots. And if they knew what (reward) there is in going early to the prayer, they would race to it. And if they knew what (reward) there is in the Isha and Fajr prayers, they would surely come to them even if they had to crawl."""
"5340","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If people knew what (reward) there is in the Isha prayer and the Fajr prayer, they would surely come to them even if they had to crawl."""
"5341","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would travel alone at night."""
"5342","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If the one who begs knew what (harm) there is for him in it, he would not beg at all."""
"5343","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will certainly come upon my Ummah what came upon the Children of Israel, as one shoe of a pair resembles the other. And the Children of Israel split into seventy-two sects, and my Ummah will split into seventy-three sects; all of them will be in the Fire except one sect: that which is upon the way on which I and my Companions are."""
"5344","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will certainly come upon the people when a person will not care whether the wealth he has acquired is from what is lawful or from what is unlawful."""
"5345","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A time will certainly come upon the people when a man will go about with charity of gold, but he will not find anyone who will accept it from him; and a single man will be seen with forty women following him, seeking refuge with him because of the scarcity of men and the abundance of women."""
"5346","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This stone will come on the Day of Resurrection having two eyes with which it sees and a tongue with which it speaks, and it will bear witness in favour of whoever touched it in truth."""
"5347","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let every man take hold of the head-rope of his mount, for this is a place where Satan came to us."""
"5348","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let each of you eat with his right hand, drink with his right hand and take with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand, drinks with his left hand, gives with his left hand and takes with his left hand."""
"5349","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let every man eat from his sacrificial animal."""
"5350","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the one among you who has recited the most of the Qur'an lead you in prayer."""
"5351","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""An army will certainly come to attack this House (the Ka'bah), until, when they are in a desert land, the middle part of them will be swallowed up by the earth; the front of them will call out to the rear of them, then they will all be swallowed up, and none will remain except a fugitive who will give news of them."""
"5352","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the one who is present convey this to the one who is absent."""
"5353","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the one of you who is present convey to the one who is absent: do not pray after Fajr except two rak'ahs."""
"5354","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will spend the night in eating and drinking, amusement and play, then in the morning they will rise as apes and swine."""
"5355","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should take a grateful heart, a tongue that remembers (Allah), and a believing wife who helps him in the affairs of the Hereafter."""
"5356","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let a man give charity from his sa' of wheat, and let him give charity from his sa' of dates."""
"5357","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should protect his face from the Fire, even if only with a piece of a date (given in charity)."""
"5358","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should undertake only as much of deeds as he is able to, for Allah Almighty does not tire until you yourselves tire; and keep to moderation and strive to be close to what is right."""
"5359","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will certainly wish that they had committed even more sins; these will be the people whose bad deeds Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has changed into good deeds."""
"5360","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those people who took on the responsibility of this matter (governance) will certainly wish that they had fallen from the Pleiades and had not taken responsibility for anything."""
"5361","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This House will be performed Hajj to and Umrah to even after the emergence of Gog and Magog (Ya'juj and Ma'juj)."""
"5362","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will be brought out of Hell through my intercession; they will be called 'the Jahannamiyyun' (the people of Hell)."""
"5363","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Through the intercession of a man who is not a prophet, people equal to the two tribes of Rabi'ah and Mudar will enter Paradise. I only say what I say."""
"5364","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Through the intercession of one man of my Ummah, more people than the tribe of Banu Tamim will enter Paradise."""
"5365","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seventy thousand or seven hundred thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise, holding one another by the hand; the first of them will not enter until the last of them has entered, and their faces will be (shining) like the moon on the night of the full moon."""
"5366","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seventy thousand of my Ummah will enter Paradise with no reckoning and no punishment upon them, and with every thousand there will be a further seventy thousand."""
"5367","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let him take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates and then becomes pure again; then, if he intends to divorce her, let him divorce her in a state of purity without having had intercourse with her. That is the waiting period ('iddah) according to which Allah has commanded that women be divorced."""
"5368","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some of my Companions will certainly come to me at the Pond, until, when I see them and recognise them, they will be held back before reaching me. Then I will say: 'O my Lord! My Companions, my Companions!' And it will be said to me: 'You do not know what new things they invented after you.'"""
"5369","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no one to whom praise is dearer than it is to Allah, and there is no one who accepts excuses more than Allah."""
"5370","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no one more patient over (hurtful words) he hears than Allah Almighty. People claim that He has a son and they set up partners with Him, yet despite that He grants them well-being and provides for them."""
"5371","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no one more excellent in the sight of Allah than a believer who is granted a long life in Islam, because of his saying Allahu Akbar, al-Hamdu lillah, Subhan Allah and La ilaha illallah."""
"5372","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever of my Ummah supports three daughters or three sisters and treats them well, they will be a screen for him from the Fire."""
"5373","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Being told (of something) is not like seeing it."""
"5374","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Being told is not like seeing: Allah Almighty informed Musa of what his people had done with the calf, yet he did not throw down the tablets; but when he saw for himself what they had done, he threw down the tablets and they broke."""
"5375","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The strong one is not the one who throws others down in wrestling; the strong one is only the one who controls himself at the time of anger."""
"5376","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting is not merely abstaining from eating and drinking; fasting is abstaining from idle and obscene talk. So if anyone insults you or behaves ignorantly towards you, say: 'I am fasting, I am fasting.'"""
"5377","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Richness (wealth) is not having an abundance of goods; rather, richness is the richness of the soul."""
"5378","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fajr is not the whiteness that appears elongated (vertically) in the horizon; rather, it is the redness that spreads across the horizon."""
"5379","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is not a liar who makes peace between people, conveying good words and saying good things for that purpose."""
"5380","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is not a believer whose neighbour is not safe from his harm."""
"5381","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The believer is not one who taunts, nor one who curses, nor one who is indecent, nor one who is foul-mouthed."""
"5382","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is not a believer who eats his fill while his neighbour beside him is hungry."""
"5383","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The poor person (miskin) is not the one who is turned away by a morsel or two; rather, the poor person is the one who has no wealth, who feels shy, and does not ask people persistently."""
"5384","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The poor person (miskin) is not the one who goes around to people and is turned away with a morsel or two, or a date or two; rather, the poor person is the one who does not find enough wealth to make him self-sufficient, and no one notices him so that charity might be given to him, and he does not himself stand up and ask people."""
"5385","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who maintains the ties of kinship is not the one who merely reciprocates; rather, the one who maintains the ties of kinship is the one who, when his ties of kinship are cut, joins them."""
"5386","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are not held in low esteem by your family. If you wish, I will spend seven days with you and then seven days each with my other wives; and if you wish, I will stay three days and then go round (to my wives) in turn."""
"5387","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is not a believer whose neighbour is not safe from his evils."""
"5388","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Between the servant and shirk there is nothing but abandoning prayer; so when he abandons it, he has committed shirk."""
"5389","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no prophet between me and 'Isa, and he is going to descend. So when you see him, recognise him: a man of medium height, of a reddish-white complexion; he will descend wearing two light yellow garments; it will seem as though water is dripping from his head even though no moisture has touched it. He will fight people for the sake of Islam, break the cross, kill the swine and abolish the jizyah; and Allah will destroy all religions in his time except Islam, and he will destroy al-Masih al-Dajjal. Then he will remain on the earth for forty years, then he will pass away, and the Muslims will offer the funeral prayer over him."""
"5390","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing heavier in the Scale than good character."""
"5391","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing in obedience to Allah Almighty that brings reward more swiftly than maintaining the ties of kinship, and there is nothing that brings punishment more swiftly than oppression and severing the ties of kinship; and a false oath leaves homes desolate."""
"5392","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing more honoured in the sight of Allah Almighty than supplication (du'a)."""
"5393","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing except that it is more obedient to Allah Almighty than the son of Adam."""
"5394","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing that is better than a thousand of its like, except man."""
"5395","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing of a human being that does not decay, except one bone, and that is the tip of the tailbone; from it the whole creation will be reassembled on the Day of Resurrection."""
"5396","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no part of the body except that it complains of the sharpness (foulness) of the tongue."""
"5397","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will be no more distress upon your father after today."""
"5398","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's divorce does not take effect in what he does not own, nor does emancipation take effect in what he does not own, nor does a sale take effect in what he does not own."""
"5399","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Janabah (major ritual impurity) has no effect on water."""
"5400","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no punishment of cutting off the hand for one who snatches something stealthily."""
"5401","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no charity (zakah) due from a Muslim on his slave or his horse."""
"5402","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no punishment of cutting off the hand for the plunderer, nor for the one who snatches something stealthily, nor for the one who betrays a trust."""
"5403","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Shaving the head is not required of women; rather, all that is required of women is to trim the hair a little."""
"5404","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A vow is not binding on a man in what he does not own; cursing a believer is like killing him; whoever kills himself with something will be punished with that very thing on the Day of Resurrection; whoever swears falsely by a religion other than Islam will be just as he said; and whoever accuses a believer of disbelief, that is like killing him."""
"5405","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Friday prayer is not obligatory on a traveller."""
"5406","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Nothing of the sin of his parents falls upon a child born of fornication."""
"5407","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ghusl is not obligatory on her (the woman) until she has an emission, just as ghusl is not obligatory on the man until he has an emission."""
"5408","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you have washed your deceased, a ritual bath (ghusl) is not then obligatory on you for it, because your deceased is not impure; it is sufficient for you to wash your hands."""
"5409","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on the awqas (the amounts between one threshold and the next)."""
"5410","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing in Paradise of what is in this world except the names."""
"5411","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on vegetables."""
"5412","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on horses and slaves, except Sadaqat al-Fitr on slaves."""
"5413","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no charity due on a slave except Sadaqat al-Fitr."""
"5414","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no retaliation (qisas) for a head wound that reaches the brain."""
"5415","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no negligence in missing a prayer by sleeping; negligence is only when awake, that you delay a prayer until the time of the next prayer has begun."""
"5416","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on less than five wasq of dates, there is no zakah on fewer than five camels, and there is no zakah on less than five uqiyah of silver."""
"5417","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on less than five wasq of dates or grain."""
"5418","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no zakah on fewer than five camels, and there is nothing on four. When they reach five, one goat is due on them, until they reach nine. When they reach ten, two goats are due, until they reach fourteen. When they reach fifteen, three goats are due, until they reach nineteen. When they reach twenty, four goats are due, until they reach twenty-four. When they reach twenty-five, one 'bint makhad' is due, up to thirty-five; if there is no 'bint makhad', then a male 'ibn labun'. If they exceed that by one camel, a 'bint labun' is due, until they reach forty-five. If they exceed that by one camel, a 'hiqqah' is due, until they reach sixty. If they exceed that by one camel, a 'jadha'ah' is due, until they reach seventy-five. If they exceed that by one camel, two 'bint labun' are due, until they reach ninety. If they exceed that by one camel, two 'hiqqahs' are due, until they reach one hundred and twenty. Then, for every fifty, one 'hiqqah', and for every forty, one 'bint labun'."""
"5419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No one has any superiority over another except through religion or righteous deeds. It is enough (evil) for a man that he be shameless, foul-tongued, miserly and cowardly."""
"5420","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no inheritance for a killer."""
"5421","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing for the killer. If he (the slain) has no heir, then his heir is the person closest to him, and the killer inherits nothing at all."""
"5422","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is nothing of the inheritance for the killer."""
"5423","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has no partner."""
"5424","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible for a woman to spend anything of her wealth without her husband's permission."""
"5425","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not fitting for women to walk in the middle of the road."""
"5426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The evil example is not for us: the one who takes back his gift is like the dog that returns to its vomit."""
"5427","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not for me to enter a decorated house."""
"5428","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting while travelling is not part of righteousness."""
"5429","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fasting while travelling is not part of righteousness, so take the concession that Allah has granted you; accept it."""
"5430","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no town that the Dajjal will not tread upon, except Makkah and Madinah. There will be no pass among its passes but that angels will stand upon it in ranks, guarding it. He will camp in the salt marsh, and Madinah will shake with its inhabitants three times, and every disbeliever and hypocrite will go out of it to him."""
"5431","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Any man who knowingly attributes himself to someone other than his father has committed disbelief. Whoever claims what is not his is not one of us, and let him take his seat in the Fire. Whoever calls a man a disbeliever or says 'enemy of Allah' while he is not so, it will come back upon himself. And let no man accuse another of sinfulness or of disbelief, for if his companion is not so, the accusation will rebound upon himself."""
"5432","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is no deed of a day except that it is sealed. When the believer falls ill, the angels say: 'O our Lord! You have held back Your servant so-and-so (with illness).' The Lord says: 'Keep sealing for him the like of his (previous) deeds until he recovers or dies.'"""
"5433","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""She is not one of us, the woman who imitates men, nor is he one of us, the man who imitates women."""
"5434","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever imitates others besides us is not one of us. Do not imitate the Jews or the Christians, for the greeting of the Jews is gesturing with the fingers, and the greeting of the Christians is gesturing with the palms."""
"5435","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever takes an evil omen or for whom an evil omen is taken, or who practises soothsaying or for whom soothsaying is practised, or who practises magic or for whom magic is practised, is not one of us."""
"5436","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever swears by the trust (amanah) is not one of us, and whoever turns a man's wife or his slave against him is not one of us."""
"5437","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever turns a woman against her husband or a slave against his master is not one of us."""
"5438","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever raises his voice (in wailing), whoever shaves his head, and whoever tears his clothes is not one of us."""
"5439","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever acts upon the way of others besides us is not one of us."""
"5440","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever cheats is not one of us."""
"5441","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever strikes the cheeks at a time of calamity, tears open the collar of his garment and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah is not one of us."""
"5442","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not recite the Qur'an in a beautiful voice is not one of us."""
"5443","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not honour our elders, does not show mercy to our young, and does not recognise the right of our scholar, is not one of us."""
"5444","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy to our young and does not recognise the standing of our elders is not one of us."""
"5445","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not show mercy to our young and does not respect our elders is not one of us."""
"5446","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The people of Paradise will not grieve over anything as much as over an hour that passed them by in which they did not remember Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"5447","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Drought does not mean that you receive no rain; rather, drought is that you receive rain, abundant rain, yet the earth grows nothing at all."""
"5448","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should say 'Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un (We belong to Allah and to Him we return)' over everything, even over (the breaking of) the strap of his sandal, for that too is among calamities."""
"5449","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should make himself independent of people, even if only by a twig of siwak."""
"5450","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The rider should greet the one walking, the one walking should greet the one sitting, and the smaller number should greet the larger number. Whoever returns the greeting, the reward is his, and whoever does not return it has nothing."""
"5451","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man from the tribe of Qahtan will drive the people with a staff."""
"5452","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A group of people may share in one sacrificial animal (hady)."""
"5453","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will drink wine and call it by a name other than its real name."""
"5454","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will drink wine and call it by a name other than its real name, and gatherings of musical instruments and singing girls will be held over their heads. Allah will cause the earth to swallow them and will turn some of them into apes and swine."""
"5455","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should pray while he is energetic; when he feels lazy or tired, let him sit down."""
"5456","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should pray in the mosque nearest to him and should not go chasing after distant mosques."""
"5457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people will certainly be touched by a scorch of the Fire as punishment for sins they committed; then Allah will admit them to Paradise by the grace of His mercy, and they will be called 'the Jahannamiyyun (the people of Hell)'."""
"5458","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Each of you should place in front of him something like the back post of a camel saddle; then whoever passes in front of him will not harm him."""
"5459","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let the Muslims be consoled in their calamities by the calamity of me (my death)."""
"5460","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""After me, trials will certainly cover my Ummah like portions of the dark night. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening, and some people will sell their religion for a small amount of worldly goods."""
"5461","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will flee from the Dajjal and take refuge in the mountains."""
"5462","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The son of Maryam will kill the Dajjal at the gate of Ludd."""
"5463","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people of my Ummah will recite the Qur'an, yet they will pass out of Islam just as an arrow passes right through the body of the game."""
"5464","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For each of you, a servant and a mount from this world are sufficient."""
"5465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For a man among you, the like of a traveller's provisions for the journey should be sufficient."""
"5466","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There will certainly be people in my Ummah who will regard khazz (silk-blend cloth), silk, wine and musical instruments as lawful. And some people will camp at the foot of a mountain; their livestock will return to them in the evening, and a needy man will come to them, and they will say to him: Come back to us tomorrow. Then Allah will bring the mountain down upon them by night, and will turn some others into apes and swine until the Day of Resurrection."""
"5467","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In this Ummah there will certainly be sinking into the earth, pelting (with stones) and transformation (of forms), and that will be when people drink wine, keep singing girls and play musical instruments."""
"5468","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night of the Mi'raj I saw Musa; he was a slender man, as though he were one of the men of (the tribe of) Shanu'ah. And I saw Isa; he was a man of medium height with a reddish complexion, as though he had just come out of a bathhouse. And I saw Ibrahim, and of all his descendants I resemble him the most. Then two vessels were brought to me, one containing milk and the other wine, and it was said to me: Drink whichever of them you wish. So I took the milk and drank it, and it was said to me: You have attained the fitrah (natural disposition). Listen! Had you taken the wine, your Ummah would have gone astray."""
"5469","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night I was taken on the Mi'raj, I did not pass by any group of angels but that they instructed me to have cupping done."""
"5470","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One night of hospitality for a guest is a right upon every Muslim. So whichever guest spends the night in someone's courtyard until morning, that hospitality is a debt owed to him by that host; if he wishes he may claim it, and if he wishes he may leave it."""
"5471","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is in the last ten nights of Ramadan, on the fifth or the third odd night."""
"5472","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is a bright night, neither hot nor cold, and no star is shot in it. And a sign of its day is that the sun rises without rays."""
"5473","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh or the twenty-ninth night. On that night the angels on the earth are more numerous than the number of pebbles."""
"5474","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is the twenty-seventh night."""
"5475","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Laylat al-Qadr is a gentle and open night, neither hot nor cold. On its morning the sun rises weak and red."""
"5476","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Let those of you who have intellect and understanding stand closest to me, then those after them, then those after them. And do not differ among yourselves, lest your hearts differ, and beware of the clamour of the marketplaces."""
"5477","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Of every two men, let one of them go forth, and the reward will be shared between them both."""
"5478","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The knots of Islam will certainly be undone, one by one."""
"5479","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people must certainly stop raising their eyes towards the sky during supplication in the prayer, or else their sight will be snatched away."""
"5480","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people must certainly stop abandoning the Friday prayers, or else Allah will set a seal upon their hearts, and then they will be among the heedless."""
"5481","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people who raise their eyes towards the sky in the prayer must certainly stop doing so, or else their sight will not return to them."""
"5482","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people who boast about their dead forefathers must certainly stop doing so; those forefathers are but the coal of Hell. Otherwise, they will become more insignificant in the sight of Allah than the dung beetle that rolls filth with its nose. Indeed, Allah has removed from you the arrogance of the Jahiliyyah and its boasting about forefathers. A person is either a God-fearing believer or a wretched sinner. All people are the children of Adam, and Adam was created from dust."""
"5483","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man should help his brother whether he is an oppressor or oppressed. If he is an oppressor, he should stop him from oppression, for that is his help; and if he is oppressed, he should help him."""
"5484","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the Day of Resurrection, the people who lived in well-being will certainly wish that their skins had been cut with scissors, when they see the reward of the people of affliction."""
"5485","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man will certainly wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades (al-Thurayya) and had not taken charge of any of the affairs of the people."""
"5486","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Soon a man will wish that he had fallen from the Pleiades (al-Thurayya) and had not taken charge of any of the affairs of the people."""
"5487","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The delaying (of repayment) by one who is able to repay a debt makes lawful (the violation of) his honour and his punishment."""
"5488","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Seeing milk in a dream is a sign of the fitrah (natural disposition)."""
"5489","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lahd (niche grave) is for us, and the shaqq (trench grave) is for others."""
"5490","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The lahd (niche grave) is for us, and the shaqq (trench grave) is for the People of the Book other than us."""
"5491","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who misses the Asr prayer is as though his family and his wealth have been snatched away from him."""
"5492","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who does not complete his bowing (ruku') and pecks in his prostration is like a hungry person who eats one or two dates, which do not benefit him at all."""
"5493","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who does not sleep until he has prayed witr is prudent."""
"5494","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills himself by strangling himself will keep strangling himself in Hell, and whoever kills himself by stabbing himself will keep stabbing himself in Hell."""
"5495","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The example of one who begs without need is like that of a person picking up live embers."""
"5496","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who drinks from a silver vessel is only gulping down the fire of Hell into his belly."""
"5497","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who recites the Qur'an and is proficient in it will be with the noble, righteous scribes (the angels), and the one who recites it while it is difficult for him will have a double reward."""
"5498","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Recreation is permissible in three things: training your horse, shooting with your bow, and playing with your wife."""
